          "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be the double dual and\nlet <MATH_0002> be the image of the evaluation map\n<MATH_0003>. Then we have a short exact\nsequence\n<MATH_0004>\nSince <MATH_0005> is normal, the local rings <MATH_0006> are discrete\nvaluation rings for points of codimension <MATH_0007> (see\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0001>).\nHence <MATH_0008> for such points by\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThus <MATH_0009> is supported in finitely many closed points and is\nglobally generated by\nCohomology of Schemes, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nWe obtain the exact sequence\n<MATH_0010>\nbecause <MATH_0011> is generated by global sections\n(Resolution of Surfaces, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nSince <MATH_0012> is an isomorphism over the complement of the\nclosed point, and since <MATH_0013> is reflexive, we see that the maps\n<MATH_0014>\ninduce isomorphisms after localization at any nonmaximal prime of <MATH_0015>.\nHence these maps are isomorphisms by More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0005>\nand the fact that reflexive modules over normal rings have property <MATH_0016>\n(More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0006>).\nThus we conclude that <MATH_0017> as desired.\n",
